You are implementing multi-provider BYOK (Bring Your Own Key) support for an Android app (Kotlin/Java). The codebase is at `<REDACTED:home>/workspace/termux-app`.

## Goal
Currently only Azure is supported as a BYOK provider. Add support for: **GitHub Copilot**, **Anthropic**, and **OpenAI**.

## Design (keep it simple)
- Each provider needs only an API key (plus an optional endpoint for OpenAI/Azure).
- Use a generic `ByokProfile` with `providerType`, `endpoint` (optional), and `apiKey` fields.
- Keep backward compatibility — existing `AzureProfile` class should remain for existing tests.

## Files to change

### 1. `app/src/main/java/com/termux/app/OpenClawByokStore.java`

Add a `ByokProvider` enum and a `ByokProfile` class. Keep `AzureProfile` for backward compat.

```java
// New ByokProvider enum (inside OpenClawByokStore)
enum ByokProvider {
    AZURE("Azure"),
    GITHUB_COPILOT("GitHub Copilot"),
    ANTHROPIC("Anthropic"),
    OPENAI("OpenAI");

    final String label;
    ByokProvider(String label) { this.label = label; }
}

// New generic ByokProfile (inside OpenClawByokStore)
static final class ByokProfile {
    final ByokProvider provider;
    final String endpoint;   // required for AZURE, optional for OPENAI, unused for GITHUB_COPILOT/ANTHROPIC
    final String resourceName; // only for AZURE
    final String apiKey;     // required for all

    ByokProfile(ByokProvider provider, String endpoint, String resourceName, String apiKey) { ... }

    boolean isValid() {
        if (apiKey is empty) return false;
        if (provider == AZURE) return endpoint and resourceName are non-empty;
        return true;
    }

    // Helper to get display label for the endpoint field
    String endpointFieldLabel() {
        switch (provider) {
            case OPENAI: return "OpenAI base URL (optional)";
            case AZURE: return "Azure endpoint";
            default: return "";
        }
    }

    boolean needsEndpoint() {
        return provider == AZURE || provider == OPENAI;
    }

    boolean needsResourceName() {
        return provider == AZURE;
    }
}
```

Add new SharedPreferences keys for the generic profile:
- `KEY_PROVIDER` = `"configured.provider"` (store enum name as string)
- Reuse existing `KEY_CONFIGURED_ENDPOINT`, `KEY_CONFIGURED_RESOURCE`, `KEY_CONFIGURED_API_KEY`

Add methods:
- `static void saveByokProfile(Context, ByokProfile)` — saves provider + credentials
- `static ByokProfile getByokProfile(Context)` — reads provider + credentials; returns null if no api key
- `static boolean hasByokProfile(Context)` — returns true if api key is set

Keep `saveConfiguredProfile(Context, AzureProfile)` and `getConfiguredProfile(Context)` for backward compat.

### 2. `app/src/main/java/ai/openclaw/app/ui/byok/ByokModels.kt`

Add a `ByokProvider` enum mirroring the Java one:
